  "query_preview": "../Sunday to Thursday/...A front will move eastward \nacross the Gulf and into the panhandle late Saturday through the\nday Sunday, bringing an end to the dry clear period on Saturday.\nThis will bring moderate to heavy rain into the NE Gulf Coast\nSunday, including the Yakutat area with around 1 to 2 inches in 24\nhours, with the rest of the panhandle expecting to see generally\nless than an inch of rain Sunday as the majority of the moisture\nis directed into the N coastline. Gusty winds will follow as well,\nmainly impacting the NE Gulf coast and northern panhandle for this\nfirst feature. Following this will be a low swinging up from the\nsouth into the Haida Gwaii area Monday, bringing some elevated\nwinds into the southern panhandle alongside moderate rain. This\nlow will push the rainfall northward later Monday into Tuesday\nmorning, however it will begin to fall apart and bring lighter\nrainfall amounts for areas north of Frederick Sound. Still not\nexpecting much overall for this quick moving low, with 0.5 to 1.5\ninches in 24 hrs expected for the southern panhandle and around \n0.6 inches or less for areas further northward. \n\nStill looking ahead to the next, larger system that is expected \nto develop in the western Gulf midweek. Uncertainty remains in the\nforecast with it being further ahead in time, looking to still \nnot impact the panhandle until Wednesday evening through Thursday,\nwith the setup and location of the low center still being quite\ndifferent across guidance. Updates will be made as the system gets\ncloser in time and as confidence grows in the expected rain and \nwind impacts.",
